# /etc/goblin-ledger/collector.env (mode 0640, owner root, group goblin). Never commit the real file.
# The "Goldline Forever" Battle.net client (the same values as the GitHub secrets BNET_CLIENT_ID and BNET_CLIENT_SECRET).
BNET_CLIENT_ID=
BNET_CLIENT_SECRET=
# A fine-grained GitHub token for kevincaron28/Trading-Wow only, permission "Contents: Read and write", to push the
# data branch. Give it an expiry date and note it in your calendar.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Optional: Cloudflare R2 copy of the data (docs/R2_DATA.md). All four, or none.
#R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
#R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
#R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
#R2_BUCKET=goblin-ledger-data
# Optional: collect from another branch of the collector code (default main).
#GOBLIN_APP_REF=main
# Optional: post the daily, weekly and monthly recaps to a Discord channel (docs/COLLECTOR_VM.md, "Discord recaps").
# Paste the channel's webhook URL; it is a secret (anyone with it can post in the channel).
#DISCORD_RECAP_WEBHOOK=
# Auction houses to post, comma separated (113 = PvP Horde), and the language (fr or en).
#DISCORD_RECAP_HOUSES=113
#DISCORD_RECAP_LANG=fr
# Optional: AI-written market summaries for the recaps (collector/recap-ai.ts; docs/COLLECTOR_VM.md, "Recap
# summaries"). Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint; all three, or none (then the template summary is used). The key is a
# secret: never commit it.
#RECAP_AI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
#RECAP_AI_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest
#RECAP_AI_API_KEY=
